   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "רָקַק – וְהִגִּיעַ בּוֹ הָרוֹק, וְהֶעֱבִיר כּוּ׳. אָמַר רַב פָּפָּא: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא בּוֹ, אֲבָל בְּבִגְדוֹ – לָא. וְנִיהְוֵי כִּי בִיֵּישׁ בִּדְבָרִים!",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches (90a): If he «spat» at him «and» his «spittle reached him, or» if «he removed» another’s cloak, he must give the injured party four hundred dinars. «Rav Pappa says: They taught» this halakha «only» in a case where the spittle reached «him. But» if the spittle landed «on his clothing» without touching him, he is «not» required to pay him. The Gemara asks: Why not? «Let it be like» one who «humiliated» another «with words.»"
  }
